course: dictionary
lesson: 5118
title: The word introduction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An introduction is a beginning. It is the first part of a story, essay or talk, and it tells you what the rest will be about. Writers use it to grab the reader's attention. «A good introduction grabs the reader.» Here, introduction means the opening part of a piece of writing.
explain: You also make an introduction when you tell people each other's names. «Mum, this is my friend Sam.» That is an introduction, and it helps people who have never met to start talking. When someone introduces themselves, you can answer "Nice to meet you" to finish it.
explain: Introduction has other meanings too. Bringing something new into use or into a place for the first time is an introduction. A first, simple lesson about a subject is an introduction to that subject. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning fits.
fact: An introduction is the first part of a book, story, essay or talk.
fact: Making an introduction means telling people each other's names so they can meet.
fact: «DUzhe pryYEmno» means nice to meet you, said after introductions; the answer is «meni tezh», which means me too.
fact: Introduction can also mean bringing something new into use or into a place for the first time.
fact: In science, introducing a new animal to a place, like rabbits to Australia, can harm nature.
exercise: «The introduction to the book tells us who the main character is.» What is an introduction here? | A list of words to learn | A picture on the cover | The last page of a book | *The first part of a book that says what it will be about
exercise: Mum says, «Sam, this is my friend Ava.» What is happening? | *People are being introduced so they can meet | A new animal is being brought to a farm | Mum is giving a long talk | A story is ending
exercise: Which phrase means a short first lesson about a subject? | A loud whisper | *A brief introduction to the subject | A happy ending | A letter of conclusion
test: When someone says "Nice to meet you", what is a good reply? | Slowly and softly | *Me too | Goodbye for ever | Rabbits in Australia
test: In science, why can introducing a new animal to a place be a problem? | It stops all the rain | It makes the animal fly | *It can harm nature | It means the animal is famous
exam: Which meaning fits «a good introduction grabs the reader»? | A final song | A way of telling names at a party | *The opening part of a piece of writing | A new animal in a zoo
